Summary: Activate a window that gains Mac focus without asking it with a simulated WM_MOUSEACTIVATE
Category: input
Kind: fix
Origin: winehq
  Version: 10.6
  Commit: b568eaac4aeb307d289ae6992457411adce6068e
  Bugs: 48121
  Authors: Rémi Bernon
  URL: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/commit/b568eaac4aeb307d289ae6992457411adce6068e
  Changes: the same change in CrossOver's text: the old if-block's braces
    are kept, with CrossOver's hack comment, instead of being unindented
Origin: crossover
  Version: 25.1.1
  CW-Hacks: 18896
  Files: dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
  Changes: only the window.c part. CrossOver's hack also changed
    cocoa_window.m (WINDOW_GOT_FOCUS for focus changes Wine makes itself);
    that part was dropped on 2026-11-26 (no program known, WineHQ never
    took it, and WineHQ master removes that event).
  Note: Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: its macdrv_window_got_focus makes no
    NtUserGetAncestor or NtUserMessageCall call (125 vs 142 instructions,
    function comparison 2026-11-15)
Upstream: yes (Wine 10.6; b568eaac4aeb)
Needed until: 10.6 (WineHQ b568eaac4aeb)
Why: When a Mac window gained focus, the Mac driver sent it a simulated
 WM_MOUSEACTIVATE (a click on its menu, HTMENU) to ask whether it wanted to
 be activated. Windows sends no such message on alt-tab or
 SetForegroundWindow, and Unity only reactivates when the last
 WM_MOUSEACTIVATE hit the client area, so Unity games never got focus back
 after the user switched away (WineHQ bug 48121). Now the window is
 activated without asking, as WineHQ does from 10.6.
Programs: Unity games (WineHQ bug 48121: Magic: The Gathering Arena,
 Subnautica: Below Zero, Desperados III, Yooka-Laylee and the Impossible
 Lair): no input after switching away and back
No test: needs real Cocoa focus events
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: reduced to the window.c hunk
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T013940 and T024442 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
index 115820e..7223389 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -1899,12 +1899,7 @@ void macdrv_window_got_focus(HWND hwnd, const macdrv_event *event)
 
     if (can_window_become_foreground(hwnd) && !(style & WS_MINIMIZE))
     {
-        /* simulate a mouse click on the menu to find out
-         * whether the window wants to be activated */
-        LRESULT ma = send_message(hwnd, WM_MOUSEACTIVATE,
-                                  (WPARAM)NtUserGetAncestor(hwnd, GA_ROOT),
-                                  MAKELONG(HTMENU, WM_LBUTTONDOWN));
-        if (ma != MA_NOACTIVATEANDEAT && ma != MA_NOACTIVATE)
+        /* CrossOver Hack #18896: don't send WM_MOUSEACTIVATE, it breaks Unity games */
         {
             TRACE("setting foreground window to %p\n", hwnd);
             NtUserSetForegroundWindow(hwnd);
